  "slug": "functions-augmenting-0a1b",
  "summary": "Five preprints use simulation-trained models to populate DMO halos with galaxies or to infer mass and gas fields from observations, from z~2.3 to z>6.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the use of simulation-trained or empirical models to connect dark matter structure with baryonic observables. In the forward direction, Extremely Randomized Trees and Gaussian Processes populate the 2.8 Gpc FLAMINGO-10k dark-matter-only run with a galaxy catalogue, while an empirical model predicts individual halo concentrations from assembly histories in CDM and WDM over z=0-5. A flexible model linking halo mass, stellar mass, SFR and UV magnitude is fit to JWST UV luminosity functions and angular correlations at z>6. In the inverse direction, deep learning recovers cluster mass maps and subhalo substructure from HST imaging, matching CLASH lensing, and a CNN reconstructs IGM column-density maps from noisy KCWI Lyα cubes of z~2.3 protoclusters. The new element is the breadth of redshift and observable coverage, though items differ in method and target.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
